node_modules/
.env
data/*.json
data/*.md
# The Anakin pipeline's feed IS meant to be committed (it's the static export
# the app reads, refreshed by re-running scripts/anakin_pipeline/pipeline.py
# and committing the result — not a runtime-generated cache like the rest of
# data/, which stays ignored).
!data/anakin-feed.json
coverage/
*.log
# Generated by `pnpm run sync` (locally) or the refresh-and-deploy workflow
# (in CI) — this is what the static site actually serves, but it's a build
# output regenerated on every sync/deploy, not something to hand-maintain
# or diff in git.
public/data/
